9. Connector Strategy

9.1 External interfaces required

Interface	Purpose	Notes
Main power connector	Discharge and charger main current path	XT90 or XT60 depending current
10S balance connector	Cell-by-cell monitoring and balancing	Must expose all 11 nodes
Optional service disconnect / arming plug	Safety during installation and maintenance	Strongly recommended

9.2 Practical recommendation

For higher current systems
	•	Main connector: XT90 or anti-spark equivalent
	•	Balance connector: dedicated protected balance harness / panel breakout
	•	Arming / service disconnect: separate removable link if possible

For moderate current systems
	•	Main connector: XT60 may be adequate
	•	same balance requirements still apply

